    "body": "<h2 id=\"h_01J3P33GKF39BXB8T67P3AQJYY\">You will learn</h2>\n<p>Learn how to recover an archived flow so you can edit and use it to send messages again. A recovered flow will return to the main Flows tab view with its status set to draft. From there you can edit it and change its status to live or manual.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01J3P33GKFCK06J22RFS1GTV7T\">Recover an archived flow</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to the <strong>Flows</strong> tab. </li>\n<li>Click the <strong>Options</strong> dropdown in the top right.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>View Archived Flows</strong> to navigate to the <em>Archived</em> view.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28716066614043\" alt=\"Options dropdown in the top right of the Flows tab with the option 'View Archived Flows' selected.\">\n</li>\n<li>Click the <strong>Actions</strong> icon to the right of the flow you would like to recover.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Unarchive</strong>.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28716066618011\" alt=\"Action button clicked next to the name of a flow in the Archived tab with the Delete option selected.\">\n</li>\n<li>You can easily navigate back to the main Flows tab to view the recovered flow by clicking the <strong>Options</strong> dropdown and choosing <strong>View Unarchived Flows</strong>.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28716066621979\" alt=\"Options dropdown in the top right of the Archived view with the option 'View Unarchived Flows' selected.\">\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01J3P33GKGQPMFQTJA97NM1MQB\">Additional resources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/115002779171\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">How to archive or delete a flow</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115002779291\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">How to pause individual flow messages</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360048376172\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">How to bulk update flow statuses</a></li>\n</ul>",
    "user_segment_ids": []
  },
